---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const siteUrl = "https://akturesult.bond";
const pageUrl = `${siteUrl}/guides/aktu-carry-over-cop-back-paper`;

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      "@id": pageUrl,
      "url": pageUrl,
      "headline": "AKTU Carry-Over (COP) & Back Paper Rules: Credit Thresholds & Year Back Criteria",
      "description": "Comprehensive guide to AKTU carry-over papers (COP), the 50% credit promotion threshold, avoiding year backs, special carry-over exams (SCOP), and registration fees.",
      "datePublished": "2026-04-02T08:00:00+05:30",
      "dateModified": "2026-10-16T12:00:00+05:30",
      "author": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "akturesult.bond Student Editorial Team"
      },
      "publisher": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "akturesult.bond",
        "url": siteUrl
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "@id": `${pageUrl}/#breadcrumb`,
      "itemListElement": [
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": siteUrl },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Guides", "item": `${siteUrl}/guides` },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Carry-Over Rules", "item": pageUrl }
      ]
    }
  ]
};
---

<Layout 
  title="AKTU Carry-Over (COP) Rules, 50% Credit Rule & Fees | akturesult.bond"
  description="Master AKTU carry-over (COP) examination rules. Learn the 50% credit threshold to avoid Year Back, Special Back Paper (SCOP) eligibility, and ERP fee steps."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-black light:bg-white text-gray-400 light:text-gray-600 text-left">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      
      <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
      <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-gray-500 mb-6" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-brand-blue transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <a href="/guides" class="hover:text-brand-blue transition-colors">Guides</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <span class="text-gray-300 light:text-gray-800 font-semibold truncate">Carry-Over Rules</span>
      </nav>

      <!-- Header -->
      <div class="border-b border-canvas-dark-border light:border-canvas-light-border pb-6 mb-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-brand-blue font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">
          <span>Examination Regulations</span>
          <span>•</span>
          <span>8 min read</span>
          <span>•</span>
          <span>Updated October 2026</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white light:text-ink leading-tight">
          AKTU Carry-Over (COP) &amp; Back Paper Rules Explained
        </h1>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-gray-400 light:text-gray-600 mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          Got a back paper in your AKTU results? Learn how Carry-Over Papers (COP) work, how to satisfy the mandatory 50% credit threshold to avoid a Year Back, and how to register on ERP.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Mandatory Non-Affiliation Alert -->
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-amber-500/30 bg-amber-500/10 text-amber-200 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed mb-10">
        <strong>Important Student Notice:</strong> akturesult.bond is an independent student utility platform and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or officially connected to Dr. A.P.J. Abdul Kalam Technical University (AKTU). This regulatory breakdown is based on the official AKTU Bachelor of Technology Ordinances.
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-10 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
        
        <!-- Section 1 -->
        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white light:text-ink">
            1. What is a Carry-Over Paper (COP)?
          </h2>
          <p>
            In AKTU, failing a course (scoring less than 30% in external theory or less than 40% aggregate) results in a letter grade <strong>'F'</strong>. Rather than forcing you to repeat the entire semester, the university allows you to "carry over" the subject and retake the written examination in a future term alongside your regular coursework.
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li><strong>Odd Semester Backs:</strong> Retaken during subsequent odd semester examination sessions (e.g., 3rd semester back retaken during 5th or 7th semester).</li>
            <li><strong>Even Semester Backs:</strong> Retaken during subsequent even semester sessions (e.g., 2nd semester back retaken during 4th or 6th semester).</li>
            <li><strong>Sessional Marks Preservation:</strong> Your original internal sessional marks awarded by your college are permanently retained; you only re-sit the external written exam.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 2 -->
        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white light:text-ink">
            2. The 50% Credit Rule &amp; Year Back (YB) Avoidance
          </h2>
          <p>
            While you can carry back papers into higher semesters, progression to the next academic year is subject to the strict <strong>50% Credit Rule</strong>:
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs border border-canvas-dark-border light:border-canvas-light-border rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
              <thead class="bg-canvas-dark-surface light:bg-canvas-light-surface text-white light:text-ink">
                <tr>
                  <th class="p-3 border-b border-canvas-dark-border">Progression Stage</th>
                  <th class="p-3 border-b border-canvas-dark-border">Mandatory Academic Requirement</th>
                  <th class="p-3 border-b border-canvas-dark-border">Penalty if Failed</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="divide-y divide-canvas-dark-border/40 light:divide-canvas-light-border">
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-brand-blue">1st Year &rarr; 2nd Year</td>
                  <td class="p-3">Must earn at least <strong>50% of total credits</strong> assigned across Semester 1 and Semester 2 combined.</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-red-400">Year Back (Repeat 1st Year)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-brand-blue">2nd Year &rarr; 3rd Year</td>
                  <td class="p-3">Must earn at least 50% credits of 2nd year AND have <strong>zero uncleared back papers</strong> from 1st Year.</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-red-400">Year Back (Cannot enter 3rd Year)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-brand-blue">3rd Year &rarr; 4th Year</td>
                  <td class="p-3">Must earn at least 50% credits of 3rd year AND have <strong>zero uncleared back papers</strong> from 2nd Year.</td>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-red-400">Year Back (Cannot enter 4th Year)</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 3 -->
        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white light:text-ink">
            3. Special Carry-Over Paper (SCOP) for Final Year Students
          </h2>
          <p>
            Final-year students who have completed all 8 semesters but carry uncleared back papers do not have to wait a full year:
          </p>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-canvas-dark-border light:border-canvas-light-border bg-canvas-dark-tile light:bg-canvas-light-tile space-y-2">
            <h4 class="font-bold text-white light:text-ink">Special Carry Over Examination Rules:</h4>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 light:text-gray-600">
              AKTU conducts a special examination session (usually in September/October) exclusively for final-year pass-out students. This allows eligible graduates to clear backlogs, finalize their degree, and join campus placements or postgraduate programs without losing an academic cycle.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 4 -->
        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white light:text-ink">
            4. How to Register for COP Exams &amp; Pay Fees
          </h2>
          <p>
            When exam registration opens each semester, students must register for their back papers on the official ERP dashboard:
          </p>
          <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 text-xs text-gray-400 light:text-gray-600">
            <li>Log into your account at <a href="https://erp.aktu.ac.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-blue hover:underline font-semibold">erp.aktu.ac.in</a>.</li>
            <li>Click <strong>Examination Form Dashboard</strong>.</li>
            <li>Your regular semester subjects will appear pre-selected. Under the <strong>Carry Over Subjects</strong> table, select the specific back papers you wish to appear for.</li>
            <li>Review the examination fee (the standard university fee is typically <strong>₹1,000 per theory subject</strong>).</li>
            <li>Pay the fee online via the integrated university payment gateway (Net Banking / Debit Card / UPI).</li>
            <li>Download and print your examination form receipt for your records.</li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 5 -->
        <section class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white light:text-ink">
            5. Impact of COP on Degree &amp; Honours
          </h2>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/10 space-y-2">
              <strong class="text-emerald-400 text-sm block">First Division is Still Possible</strong>
              <p class="text-xs text-gray-300">
                Clearing a COP updates your marksheet. If your final cumulative CGPA is <strong>&ge; 6.50</strong>, you will still be awarded an official <strong>First Division</strong> on your graduation degree.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-red-500/30 bg-red-500/10 space-y-2">
              <strong class="text-red-400 text-sm block">Honours Eligibility is Forfeited</strong>
              <p class="text-xs text-gray-300">
                To receive "First Division with Honours" (Distinction), university ordinances mandate that every single course must be cleared in the <strong>first attempt</strong> without any back papers.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

      </div>

      <!-- Quick CTA -->
      <div class="mt-12 p-6 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-r from-brand-blue/20 to-purple-600/15 border border-brand-blue/30 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white light:text-ink">Think your paper was evaluated unfairly?</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 light:text-gray-600">Explore Stage 1 and Stage 2 Challenge Evaluation and Scrutiny procedures.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/guides/aktu-revaluation-scrutiny-challenge" class="px-4 py-2.5 rounded-xl bg-brand-blue hover:bg-brand-blue-hover text-white text-xs font-bold transition-all shadow-md shrink-0">
          Challenge Evaluation Guide &rarr;
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
